// PERSISTENT LOAD-IN — resident kernel with the real stage bodies:
//   S1 = BPX-L (bpxl.comp, LDS 4,096 B form) transplanted verbatim
//        (shared-state section + helpers + main body as bpxMain();
//        only the instance selector and the pc block became globals),
//   S2 = selection dedupe phase A (rec_dedup_m form, child-direct),
//   S3 = dedupe B + emit/order + repsOrd cache + B&B rounds
//        (prefix-P = sel_prefix4 algorithm at 64 lanes, passB =
//        bxp_b body, judge on WG 0) + final sort (sel_sort3 form),
//   S4 = materialization (sel_mat form) + next-ply scratch reset.
// Sync: skeleton grid3 barriers, 3-point basis (B1/B2/B4) with the
// dedupe barriers folded onto B2 + one extra (X1); selection-internal
// transitions X2/X3/X5 and 3 per B&B round. Contracts per
// PERSISTENT-IMPL section 6: all inter-stage buffers coherent;
// dedupe refill (scratch reset) lives in S4/init, never in S3's tail
// after the last read; anomaly = timeout flag -> whole grid exits ->
// host recomputes the decision in the basic form.
#version 460
// pfl_r15_serve.comp — generated by gen_r15_serve.py from pfl_r14_sub800.comp
// Live self-contained 15-ply persistent beam search kernel (S2 & Guideline/TBP).
// Single resident dispatch per decision (~0.6ms on RX 6400, zero post-dispatch VRAM readback).
